        }
      ],
      "answer": "In the MapleHarvest Quebec pilot, the temporary field mappings planned in the router transform include mapping txn_id to transaction_id, total_amount to amount_cents, performing type coercion from string to int, preserving key fields store_id and register_id, and adding a transformation flag field _ns_transform=true. This transform will be deployed in the SI-CLOUD-ROUTER component as a temporary fix to address schema rejections caused by mixed field names and types at store-level preprocessing. Additionally, audit logs (OR-AUDIT-LOGS) will be enabled for each transformed event to ensure compliance and rollback safety.\n\nThe March 23 workshop is a Schema Signoff Workshop with the agenda to agree on a canonical schema for payment, register_events, and sensor_thermo events; define alias mapping; and establish a producer migration plan. The deliverable from this workshop is a signed schema document to be uploaded to SI-SCHEMA-REG and a change control ticket with producer migration milestones. The workshop is scheduled for 90 minutes on 2026-03-23.\n\nThese details are from the MapleHarvest Quebec Pilot project reset and mitigation plan and related Slack discussions [art_5a91258f4056, art_6c5bb3a4b89f].",
