      "answer": "The SCIM fields conflicting at Aureum were \"department\" and \"businessUnit.\" Specifically, Merchant Services used businessUnit=merchant, while Payments Ops used department=payments. This mismatch caused the ingestion normalization to fail collapsing these into a single canonical attribute, leading to provisioning delays.\n\nJin proposed a fast fix that avoids waiting on Okta change control by adding a preprocessing rule in Signal Ingest to map businessUnit to department (or vice versa) and publish a normalized field for the correlator. This fix is a configuration-only change, hot-reloadable, and low risk, allowing immediate deployment without appliance restarts during sensitive settlement windows. The longer-term fix would be to standardize at the identity source (Okta), but that requires change control and 2\u20134 weeks lead time.\n\nThis approach was agreed upon to quickly address the provisioning lag while enabling tracing and SLA dashboarding for further diagnostics and remediation planning [art_79f625aafa16].",
