      "answer": "We have a recurring Canada approval-bypass pattern across multiple accounts, not just MapleBridge Insurance. The customers sharing this pattern are City of Verdant Bay, Maple Regional Transit Authority, MapleBay Marketplace, MapleFork Franchise Systems, MaplePath Career Institute, MapleWest Bank, and MapleBridge Insurance.\n\nThe shared failure pattern in plain English is: After migrating from legacy workflow tooling to the current Orchestrator system, approval workflows for Canada-specific policies fail because the rules engine evaluates global default rules with higher priority or in the wrong order, overriding or bypassing region-specific (country or province) approval policies. This causes approvals to get stuck, auto-denied, bypassed, or routed incorrectly, leading to manual overrides, backlogs, and compliance risks. The root causes include schema normalization issues, delayed schema registry synchronization, and lack of explicit precedence metadata in the rules engine. Fixes involve adjusting rule evaluation precedence to prioritize region-specific overrides over global defaults, deploying override rules to force manual approvals, enabling audit logs, and providing evidence exports for compliance.\n\nMapleBridge Insurance is not a one-off case; it shares the same pattern of approval bypass due to rule precedence conflicts after migration, similar to the other Canadian customers listed.\n\nThis recurring pattern is documented across these multiple Canadian customers, indicating a systemic issue rather than isolated incidents [art_cbfb5f92862c, art_6be1b68b59cb, art_39c1434aa40a, art_f4a8c516b934, art_e9c20e0a23e0, art_981952a71434, art_b86a0ca2ce1e, art_ad58f3ce1afd, art_54e35e2cb431, art_e697b3abe158].",
